### Quick Facts
| Item | Details |
|------|---------|
| **Official name** | Etihad Stadium (also called the City of Manchester Stadium) |
| **Location** | Ashton New Rd, Manchester M11 3FF, United Kingdom |
| **Home team** | Manchester City Football Club |
| **Opened** | 2002 (built for the Commonwealth Games) |
| **Seating capacity** | 53,400 (expandable to ~60,000 for concerts) |
| **Architects** | Arup & Buro Happold – sleek modern façade, acoustically‑tuned roof |
| **Website** | https://www.mancity.com/etihadstadium |
| **Phone** | +44 161 555 5555 |
| **Average rating** | ★ 4.7 / 5 (≈ 1,200+ reviews) |
| **Nearby transport** | Metrolink tram – **Etihad Campus** stop (line 2); bus routes 50, 59, 64, 67, 69, 191, 197 |

---

## Why Visit?  
- **World‑class football venue** – home of one of the Premier League’s most successful clubs.  
- **Multi‑purpose arena** – hosts major concerts (Ed Sheeran, Beyoncé, etc.), community events, and other sports.  
- **State‑of‑the‑art facilities** – premium hospitality suites, a 360° cinema suite, holographic exhibition space, and a roof that delivers excellent acoustics.  
- **Etihad Stadium Museum** – interactive displays of Manchester City’s trophies, historic kits, and behind‑the‑scenes footage.  
- **Guided tours** – from a standard 45‑minute “Stadium Tour” to the premium “Legends Tour” (players’ tunnel, bench, dressing‑room access, and a photo‑op on the pitch).  

---

## 75‑Minute Etihad Stadium Guided Tour (Klook)  

| Detail | Information |
|--------|-------------|
| **Product name** | **75‑minute Etihad Stadium Guided Tour** |
| **Provider** | Klook (bookable via Klook, Booking.com, etc.) |
| **Price** | **USD 39.03** (representative price – may vary by date & currency) |
| **Cancellation** | **Free cancellation** (subject to provider’s policy) |
| **Availability** | Live‑availability check supported; tickets are bookable online. |
| **Accessibility** | Wheelchair‑accessible. |
| **On‑site requirements** | Arrive **at least 20 minutes** before the activity starts; bring the ticket (digital or printed). |
| **Age restriction** | Must be **18 years or older** to book, or be accompanied by an adult. |
| **What you’ll see** | • Players’ tunnel to the pitch <br>• Press‑conference room <br>• Home & away dressing rooms <br>• Dugouts <br>• Exhibition space with holographic content <br>• 360° cinema suite <br>• Overview of the stadium’s 53,400‑seat layout |
| **Guide** | Professional guide narrates the club’s history, achievements, and stadium design. |
| **Duration** | **75 minutes** (includes a walk through the tunnel and a brief museum entry). |
| **Typical start times** | Multiple slots per day (e.g., 10:00, 12:30, 15:00, 17:30) – check the live calendar when booking. |
| **Reviews** | ★ 5.0 (1 review on the platform – “Great experience, very informative!”) |
| **Extras** | Free‑cancellation label, live‑availability check, native‑app support for booking. |

### How to Book
1. **Visit Klook** (or the Booking.com “Attractions” section) and search for **“75‑minute Etihad Stadium Guided Tour.”**  
2. Choose a date/time that fits your itinerary.  
3. Complete the purchase – you’ll receive a digital voucher (QR code) that you present at the stadium ticket desk.  
4. **Tip:** Book at least 48 hours in advance, especially on match days when the stadium may be closed for tours.

---

## General Stadium Tour Options (Beyond the 75‑minute Klook tour)

| Tour | Duration | Highlights | Approx. Price (GBP) |
|------|----------|------------|---------------------|
| **Standard Stadium Tour** | 45 min | Players’ tunnel, dressing rooms, pitch‑side view, museum entry | £15‑£20 |
| **Legends Tour (Premium)** | 60 min | Exclusive bench seat, behind‑the‑scenes access, souvenir photo, priority museum entry | £35‑£45 |
| **Family/Group Packages** | Varies | Interactive games for kids, “mini‑coach” experience, group discounts | Custom |
| **Match‑day Experience** | Full match | Stadium entry, pre‑match hospitality, optional tour before kickoff | Varies by ticket tier |

**Booking tip:** All tours can be booked online via the official Manchester City website, Klook, or other travel‑activity platforms. Tours may be **suspended on match days** or when the stadium is booked for concerts, so always verify availability.

---

## Visiting Logistics

### Opening Hours (Tours)  
| Day | Hours |
|-----|-------|
| Monday – Friday | 09:00 – 18:00 |
| Saturday – Sunday | 10:00 – 17:00 |

*Hours can change on match days or for special events—check the website before you go.*

### Getting There
- **Metrolink tram:** Stop **Etihad Campus** (line 2) – 2‑minute walk to the stadium.  
- **Buses:** Routes 50, 59, 64, 67, 69, 191, 197 stop nearby.  
- **Car/Parking:** Surface lots and a large multi‑storey car park (pay‑and‑display).  
- **Walking/Cycling:** The stadium sits in the East Manchester “Etihad Campus” – well‑connected via pedestrian and cycle routes.

### Food & Drink
- **Stadium Café** – quick bites, coffee, soft drinks.  
- **Etihad Kitchen** – sit‑down restaurant (open during tours and match days).  
- **Bars & Lounges** – premium hospitality suites with cocktail menus for ticket‑holders.

### Shopping
- **Official Club Store** – exclusive Manchester City kits, scarves, and stadium‑branded merchandise.  
- **Pop‑up stalls** – often feature local artisan goods during events.

### Photo‑Friendly Spots
1. **Pitch‑side view** – from the tunnel (Legends Tour).  
2. **Stadium façade** – iconic night‑time lighting.  
3. **Roof terrace** – panoramic city skyline (available on select hospitality packages).  
4. **Museum exhibit** – trophy cabinet and historic kit displays.

---

## Nearby Attractions (Great for a Full Day)

| Attraction | Distance | Why Go |
|------------|----------|--------|
| **National Football Museum** | 0.8 mi | Interactive football history exhibits. |
| **Manchester Museum** | 1.2 mi | Natural history, archaeology, and more. |
| **Northern Quarter** | 1.5 mi | Trendy cafés, street art, boutique shops. |
| **Manchester Cathedral** | 2 mi | Stunning medieval architecture. |
| **Old Trafford (Manchester United)** | 3 mi | Rival stadium tour – perfect for football fans. |

---

## Practical Tips for a Smooth Visit
- **Arrive 20‑30 minutes early** – especially for guided tours (you’ll need time for ticket verification).  
- **Dress comfortably** – sneakers are ideal; you’ll be walking on concrete.  
- **Check the match schedule** – tours may be cancelled on match days or when the stadium is booked for concerts.  
- **Bring a camera** – flash may be restricted in certain areas (e.g., dressing rooms).  
- **Weather** – most tour areas are indoor, but exterior photo spots are outdoors—bring a light jacket if it’s chilly.  
- **Accessibility** – wheelchair‑friendly routes, audio‑described tours, and accessible restrooms are available.  

---

## Summary

Etihad Stadium is more than just a football ground; it’s a modern cultural hub that blends sport, architecture, and entertainment. Whether you:

- **Want a quick glimpse** of the players’ tunnel and dressing rooms (75‑minute Klook tour),  
- **Seek a deeper, premium experience** (Legends Tour), or  
- **Plan a full day** exploring Manchester’s football heritage and vibrant city life,

the stadium offers a memorable, well‑organized visit.  

**Ready to book?** Use the link below (or search “75‑minute Etihad Stadium Guided Tour” on Klook/Booking.com) to secure your spot, then enjoy the behind‑the‑scenes world of Premier League football!  

---  

**Links**  
- Official stadium site: https://www.mancity.com/etihadstadium  
- Klook tour page (search “Etihad Stadium Guided Tour”): https://www.klook.com/  
- Metrolink tram info: https://tfgm.com/metro/tram  

Feel free to ask if you need help with booking, itinerary planning, or any other travel details!

